# TEMPLATE ONLY — do not put real passwords here.
# Generate the real file with:  python scripts/generate_secrets.py
# (writes redis/users.acl with a SHA-256 password hash, and secrets/redis_url; both git-ignored)
#
# - default user disabled: unauthenticated connections are refused
# - qrguard: application user (API + worker + Celery). Dangerous/admin commands are denied
#   (FLUSHALL, FLUSHDB, CONFIG, DEBUG, KEYS, SHUTDOWN, MONITOR, ACL, ...). INFO is re-allowed.
# - "#<sha256>" stores only the hash of the password, never the plaintext.
# - Key scope is "~*" because Celery/kombu create keys with dynamic names (e.g. pidbox reply
#   queues prefixed by a UUID). Narrowing it is possible but must be validated against Celery first.
user default off
user qrguard on #REPLACE_WITH_SHA256_OF_PASSWORD ~* &* +@all -@dangerous +info
